<p id="A3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i)</annotation></semantics></math> follows by assuming that
<math id="A3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{q}_{0}(y^{i}|x_{k}^{UM})-q_{0}(y^{i}|x_{k}^{UM})=o(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{q}_{0}(y^{i}|x_{k}^{UM})-q_{0}(y^{i}|x_{k}^{UM})=o(1)</annotation></semantics></math> for all such <math id="A3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> pairs, and <math id="A3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(ii)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(ii)</annotation></semantics></math> follows because <math id="A3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{0}(y^{i}|x_{k}^{UM})&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{0}(y^{i}|x_{k}^{UM})&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, suppose that <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{t\in(\delta,T)}\mathcal{L}_{SE}(s_{t};t)\lesssim\varepsilon_{\text{score}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≲</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mtext>score</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{t\in(\delta,T)}\mathcal{L}_{SE}(s_{t};t)\lesssim\varepsilon_{\text{score}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that, for all <math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>’s,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{TV}(s;T-t_{k})\lesssim\sqrt{d(S-1)}\max\{1,(T-t_{k})^{-1}\}\cdot\sqrt{\varepsilon_{\text{score}}^{\prime}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msqrt><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mtext>score</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{TV}(s;T-t_{k})\lesssim\sqrt{d(S-1)}\max\{1,(T-t_{k})^{-1}\}\cdot\sqrt{\varepsilon_{\text{score}}^{\prime}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, given that the step-sizes are <math id="A3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{k}=\kappa\min\left\{1,T-t_{k}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{k}=\kappa\min\left\{1,T-t_{k}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the time-weighted loss satisfies</p>
<table id="A3.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{TV}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{TV}(s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}(t_{k+1}-t_{k})\sqrt{d(S-1)}\max\{1,(T-t_{k})^{-1}\}\cdot\sqrt{\varepsilon_{\text{score}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msqrt><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mtext>score</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}(t_{k+1}-t_{k})\sqrt{d(S-1)}\max\{1,(T-t_{k})^{-1}\}\cdot\sqrt{\varepsilon_{\text{score}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sqrt{d(S-1)}\sqrt{\varepsilon_{\text{score}}^{\prime}}\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}(t_{k+1}-t_{k})\max\{1,(T-t_{k})^{-1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mtext>score</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sqrt{d(S-1)}\sqrt{\varepsilon_{\text{score}}^{\prime}}\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}(t_{k+1}-t_{k})\max\{1,(T-t_{k})^{-1}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle(iii)}}{{\lesssim}}\sqrt{dS}(T+\log\delta^{-1})\cdot\sqrt{\varepsilon_{\text{score}}^{\prime}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mover><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msqrt><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mtext>score</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle(iii)}}{{\lesssim}}\sqrt{dS}(T+\log\delta^{-1})\cdot\sqrt{\varepsilon_{\text{score}}^{\prime}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="A3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(iii)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(iii)</annotation></semantics></math> follows from <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ Appendix C Proof of ‣ Sharp Convergence Rates for Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> below. Also note that <math id="A3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\asymp\log(d/\sqrt{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≍</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\asymp\log(d/\sqrt{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> under the setting of <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 3.2 Convergence Upper Bound for the Euler Method ‣ 3 Convergence Guarantees for the Euler Method ‣ Sharp Convergence Rates for Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose that <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{k+1}-t_{k}\leq\kappa\min\left\{1,T-t_{k}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{k+1}-t_{k}\leq\kappa\min\left\{1,T-t_{k}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}(t_{k+1}-t_{k})^{p}\max\left\{1,(T-t_{k+1})^{-p}\right\}\leq\kappa^{p}N." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}(t_{k+1}-t_{k})^{p}\max\left\{1,(T-t_{k+1})^{-p}\right\}\leq\kappa^{p}N.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Meanwhile, if we take <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{k+1}-t_{k}=\kappa\min\left\{1,T-t_{k}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{k+1}-t_{k}=\kappa\min\left\{1,T-t_{k}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the number of steps satisfies that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\lesssim\kappa^{-1}(T+\log\delta^{-1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≲</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\lesssim\kappa^{-1}(T+\log\delta^{-1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">See <a href="#A12.SS1" title="L.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix L Proofs of Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Sharp Convergence Rates for Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">L.1</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3.1 General Decomposition in Total Variation ‣ 3 Convergence Guarantees for the Euler Method ‣ Sharp Convergence Rates for Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To begin, note that</p>
<table id="A4.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}(\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{T-\delta},p_{T-\delta})=\mathrm{TV}(\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{0},p_{0})+\int_{0}^{T-\delta}\frac{\partial}{\partial t}\mathrm{TV}(\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t},p_{t})\mathrm{d}t." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mpadded style="width:6.5pt;height:7.1pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;" depth="0.0pt" height="7.1pt" width="6.5pt"><mover accent="true"><mpadded style="width:4.8pt;height:6.199999999999999pt;vertical-align:-1.9pt;" depth="1.9