<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(iii)}{=}\mathbb{E}_{x_{k}}\frac{1}{k}\sum_{l:x_{k}^{l}=\mathrm{[MASK]}}\mathbb{E}_{a\sim q_{0}^{l}(\cdot|x_{k}^{UM})}\left[-\log(\bar{\mu}_{\theta}^{l}(x_{k})[a])\right]-\mathbb{E}_{x_{k}}\frac{1}{k}\sum_{l:x_{k}^{l}=\mathrm{[MASK]}}H(q_{0}^{l}(\cdot|x_{k}^{UM}))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>MASK</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>MASK</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(iii)}{=}\mathbb{E}_{x_{k}}\frac{1}{k}\sum_{l:x_{k}^{l}=\mathrm{[MASK]}}\mathbb{E}_{a\sim q_{0}^{l}(\cdot|x_{k}^{UM})}\left[-\log(\bar{\mu}_{\theta}^{l}(x_{k})[a])\right]-\mathbb{E}_{x_{k}}\frac{1}{k}\sum_{l:x_{k}^{l}=\mathrm{[MASK]}}H(q_{0}^{l}(\cdot|x_{k}^{UM})),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.p11.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A10.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i)</annotation></semantics></math> follows from <a href="#Thmproposition3" title="Proposition 3. ‣ Appendix I FHS Sampling in CTMC Framework: and its Proof ‣ Sharp Convergence Rates for Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, <math id="A10.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(ii)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(ii)</annotation></semantics></math> follows because the distribution of the CTMC path implies that <math id="A10.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is independent from <math id="A10.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{i_{j}\}_{j=d}^{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{i_{j}\}_{j=d}^{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A10.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{a_{j}\}_{j=d}^{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{a_{j}\}_{j=d}^{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and hence independent from <math id="A10.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A10.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(iii)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(iii)</annotation></semantics></math> follows from (<a href="#A10.E36" title="Equation 36 ‣ Appendix J Proof of ‣ Sharp Convergence Rates for Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>), and <math id="A10.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the entropy. A key step is that two expectations <math id="A10.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tau_{k-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tau_{k-1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A10.p11.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{a\sim q_{0}^{i_{k-1}}(\cdot|x_{k}^{UM})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{a\sim q_{0}^{i_{k-1}}(\cdot|x_{k}^{UM})}</annotation></semantics></math> are interchangeable thanks to the true token-prediction distribution <math id="A10.p11.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{0}^{i_{k-1}}(\cdot|x_{k}^{UM})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{0}^{i_{k-1}}(\cdot|x_{k}^{UM})</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of time <math id="A10.p11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A10.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.p12.2" class="ltx_p">Notice that</p>
<table id="A10.E38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A10.E38X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E38X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}}\left[\mathcal{L}_{\infty}\left(x_{0}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}}\left[\mathcal{L}_{\infty}\left(x_{0}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="7" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A10.E38Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E38Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}}\sum_{k=1}^{d}\mathbb{E}_{x_{k}\sim\tilde{q}_{k|0}\left(x_{k}\mid x_{0}\right)}\frac{1}{k}\sum_{l:x_{k}^{l}=\mathrm{[MASK]}}(-\log\bar{\mu}_{\theta}\left(x_{k}\right)\left[x_{0}^{l}\right])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>MASK</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup><mo>]</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}}\sum_{k=1}^{d}\mathbb{E}_{x_{k}\sim\tilde{q}_{k|0}\left(x_{k}\mid x_{0}\right)}\frac{1}{k}\sum_{l:x_{k}^{l}=\mathrm{[MASK]}}(-\log\bar{\mu}_{\theta}\left(x_{k}\right)\left[x_{0}^{l}\right])</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A10.E38Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E38Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{d}\frac{1}{k}\mathbb{E}_{x_{0},x_{k}}\sum_{l:x_{k}^{l}=\mathrm{[MASK]}}(-\log\bar{\mu}_{\theta}\left(x_{k}\right)\left[x_{0}^{l}\right])." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>MASK</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup><mo>]</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{d}\frac{1}{k}\mathbb{E}_{x_{0},x_{k}}\sum_{l:x_{k}^{l}=\mathrm{[MASK]}}(-\log\bar{\mu}_{\theta}\left(x_{k}\right)\left[x_{0}^{l}\right]).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A10.E38Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E38Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{d}\frac{1}{k}\mathbb{E}_{x_{k}}\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\mid x_{k}}\sum_{l:x_{k}^{l}=\mathrm{[MASK]}}(-\log\bar{\mu}_{\theta}\left(x_{k}\right)\left[x_{0}^{l}\right])." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>MASK</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup><mo>]</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{d}\frac{1}{k}\mathbb{E}_{x_{k}}\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\mid x_{k}}\sum_{l:x_{k}^{l}=\mathrm{[MASK]}}(-\log\bar{\mu}_{\theta}\left(x_{k}\right)\left[x_{0}^{l}\right]).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A10.E38Xd" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E38Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{d}\frac{1}{k}\mathbb{E}_{x_{k}}\sum_{l:x_{k}^{l}=\mathrm{[MASK]}}\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\mid x_{k}}\left[-\log\bar{\mu}_{\theta}\left(x_{k}\right)\left[x_{0}^{l}\right]\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>MASK</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup><mo>]</mo><mo>]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{d}\frac{1}{k}\mathbb{E}_{x_{k}}\sum_{l:x_{k}^{l}=\mathrm{[MASK]}}\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\mid x_{k}}\left[-\log\bar{\mu}_{\theta}\left(x_{k}\right)\left[x_{0}^{l}\right]\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A10.E38Xe" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E38Xe.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{d}\frac{1}{k}\mathbb{E}_{x_{k}}\sum_{l:x_{k}^{l}=\mathrm{[MASK]}}\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}^{l}\mid x_{k}}\left[-\log\bar{\mu}_{\theta}\left(x_{k}\right)\left[x_{0}^{l}\right]\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>MASK</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup><mo>]</mo><mo>]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{d}\frac{1}{k}\mathbb{E}_{x_{k}}\sum_{l:x_{k}^{l}=\mathrm{[MASK]}}\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}^{l}\mid x_{k}}\left[-\log\bar{\mu}_{\theta}\left(x_{k}\right)\left[x_{0}^{l}\right]\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A10.E38Xf" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E38Xf.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{d}\frac{1}{k}\mathbb{E}_{x_{k}}\sum_{l:x_{k}^{l}=\mathrm{[MASK]}}\mathbb{E}_{a\sim q_{0}^{l}(\cdot|x_{k}^{UM})}\left[-\log\bar{\mu}_{\theta}\left(x_{k}\right)\left[a\right]\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>MASK</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>]</mo><mo>]</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{d}\frac{1}{k}\mathbb{E}_{x_{k}}\sum_{l:x_{k}^{l}=\mathrm{[MASK]}}\mathbb{E}_{a\sim q_{0}^{l}(\cdot|x_{k}^{UM})}\left[-\log\bar{\mu}_{\theta}\left(x_{k}\right)\left[a\right]\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.p12.3" class="ltx_p">which is precisely the first term
in (<a href="#A10.E37" title="Equation 37 ‣ Appendix J Proof of ‣ Sharp Convergence Rates for Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A10.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.p13.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, combining (<a href="#A10.E34" title="Equation 34 ‣ Appendix J Proof of ‣ Sharp Convergence Rates for Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>), (<a href="#A10.E37" title="Equation 37 ‣ Appendix J Proof of ‣ Sharp Convergence Rates for Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>), and (<a href="#A10.E38" title="Equation 38 ‣ Appendix J Proof of ‣ Sharp Convergence Rates for Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38</span></a>), we have</p>
<table id="A10.Ex155" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A10.Ex155X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex155X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}(\mathbb{P}_{\mathrm{CTMC}}(\mathrm{path})||\mathbb{P}_{\mathrm{FHS}}(\mathrm{path}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>CTMC</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>path</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>FHS</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>path</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}(\mathbb{P}_{\mathrm{CTMC}}(\mathrm{path})||\mathbb{P}_{\mathrm{FHS}}(\mathrm{path}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex155X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{k=1}^{d}\mathbb{E}_{x_{k}}\frac{1}{k}\sum_{l:x_{k}^{l}=\mathrm{[MASK]}}\mathbb{E}_{a\sim q_{0}^{l}(\cdot|x_{k}^{UM})}\left[\log(\bar{\mu}_{\theta}^{l}(x_{k})[a])\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>MASK</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{k=1}^{d}\mathbb{E}_{x_{k}}\frac{1}{k}\sum_{l:x_{k}^{l}=\mathrm{[MASK]}}\mathbb{E}_{a\sim q_{0}^{l}(\cdot|x_{k}^{UM})}\left[\log(\bar{\mu}_{\theta}^{l}(x_{k})[a])\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.Ex155Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex155Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\sum_{k=1}^{d}\mathbb{E}_{x_{k}}\frac{1}{k}\sum_{l:x_{k}^{l}=\mathrm{[MASK]}}H(q_{0}^{l}(\cdot|x_{k}^{UM}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>MASK</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\sum_{k=1}^{d}\mathbb{E}_{x_{k}}\frac{1}{k}\sum_{l:x_{k}^{l}=\mathrm{[MASK]}}H(q_{0}^{l}(\cdot|x_{k}^{UM}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.Ex155Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex155Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim q_{0}}\left[\mathcal{L}_{\infty}(x_{0})\right]-\sum_{k=1}^{d}\mathbb{E}_{x_{k}}\frac{1}{k}\sum_{l:x_{k}^{l}=\mathrm{[MASK]}}H(q_{0}^{l}(\cdot|x_{k}^{UM}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>]</mo><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>MASK</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim q_{0}}\left[\mathcal{L}_{\infty}(x_{0})\right]-\sum_{k=1}^{d}\mathbb{E}_{x_{k}}\frac{1}{k}\sum_{l:x_{k}^{l}=\mathrm{[MASK]}}H(q_{0}^{l}(\cdot|x_{k}^{UM}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.Ex155Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex155Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim q_{0}}\left[\mathcal{L}_{\infty}(x_{0})\right]-\sum_{k=1}^{d}\frac{1}{k}\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim q_{0}}\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{M}_{k}}\sum_{l\in\mathcal{M}_{k}}H\left(q_{0}^{l}(\cdot|x_{0}^{\mathcal{M}_{k}^{c}})\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>]</mo><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mi>H</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim q_{0}}\left[\mathcal{L}_{\infty}(x_{0})\right]-\sum_{k=1}^{d}\frac{1}{k}\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim q_{0}}\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{M}_{k}}\sum_{l\in\mathcal{M}_{k}}H\left(q_{0}^{l}(\cdot|x_{0}^{\mathcal{M}_{k}^{c}})\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A10.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.p14.1" class="ltx_p">Apply the equivalence between integrated <math id="A10.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{SE}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{SE}</annotation></semantics></math> and expected NELBO in <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2. ‣ 4 Convergence Guarantees for the FHS Algorithm ‣ Sharp Convergence Rates for Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, and <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 4 Convergence Guarantees for the FHS Algorithm ‣ Sharp Convergence Rates for Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, then we have</p>
<table id="A10.Ex156" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex156.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(\mathbb{P}_{\mathrm{CTMC}}(\mathrm{path})||\mathbb{P}_{\mathrm{FHS}}(\mathrm{path}))\leq\varepsilon^{\prime\prime}_{\mathrm{score}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>CTMC</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>path</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>FHS</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>path</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>score</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(\mathbb{P}_{\mathrm{CTMC}}(\mathrm{path})||\mathbb{P}_{\mathrm{FHS}}(\mathrm{path}))\leq\varepsilon^{\prime\prime}_{\mathrm{score}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A10.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.p15.1" class="ltx_p">Using the data processing inequality, we finally come to the conclusion</p>
<table id="A10.Ex157" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex157.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(q_{0}(x_{0})||\mathbb{P}_{\mathrm{FHS}}(x_{0}))\leq\mathrm{KL}(\mathbb{P}_{\mathrm{CTMC}}(\mathrm{path})||\mathbb{P}_{\mathrm{FHS}}(\mathrm{path}))\leq\varepsilon^{\prime\prime}_{\mathrm{score}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>FHS</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>CTMC</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>path</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>FHS</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>path</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>score</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(q_{0}(x_{0})||\mathbb{P}_{\mathrm{FHS}}(x_{0}))\leq\mathrm{KL}(\mathbb{P}_{\mathrm{CTMC}}(\mathrm{path})||\mathbb{P}_{\mathrm{FHS}}(\mathrm{path}))\leq\varepsilon^{\prime\prime}_{\mathrm{score}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A10.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.p16.1" class="ltx_p">The proof is now complete.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A11" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix K </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5. ‣ 4 Convergence Guarantees for the FHS Algorithm ‣ Sharp Convergence Rates for Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a></h2>

<div id="A11.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We construct both a target distribution <math id="A11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and a special form of the estimated predictive model <math id="A11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, which yield a lower error bound.</p>
</div>
<div id="A11.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A11.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To proceed, fix <math id="A11.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a},\bm{b}\in[S]^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒃</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a},\bm{b}\in[S]^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A11.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{b}^{i}\neq\bm{a}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒃</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{b}^{i}\neq\bm{a}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A11.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}^{i},\bm{b}^{i}\neq\mathrm{[MASK]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒃</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>MASK</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}^{i},\bm{b}^{i}\neq\mathrm{[MASK]}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A11.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[d]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[d]</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A11.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{0}=\bm{\delta}_{\bm{a}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝜹</mi><mi>𝒂</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{0}=\bm{\delta}_{\bm{a}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Also, for any <math id="A11.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A11.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A11.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A11.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> be as follows:</p>
<table id="A11.Ex158" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A11.Ex158.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\theta}^{i}(x_{t},t)[y^{i}]=\begin{cases}1-\rho,&amp;\text{ if }y^{i}=\bm{a}^{i},\\
\rho,&amp;\text{ if }y^{i}=\bm{b}^{i}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝒃</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\theta}^{i}(x_{t},t)[y^{i}]=\begin{cases}1-\rho,&amp;\text{ if }y^{i}=\bm{a}^{i},\\
\rho,&amp;\text{ if }y^{i}=\bm{b}^{i}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A11.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where we choose choose <math id="A11.p2.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\rho=1-e^{-\varepsilon^{\prime\prime}_{\mathrm{score}}/d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>score</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=1-e^{-\varepsilon^{\prime\prime}_{\mathrm{score}}/d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A11.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A11.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We next show that the above constructed <math id="A11.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies
<a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 4 Convergence Guarantees for the FHS Algorithm ‣ Sharp Convergence Rates for Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, i.e., <math id="A11.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{+\infty}\mathcal{L}_{SE}(s;t)\,\mathrm{d}t\leq\varepsilon^{\prime\prime}_{\mathrm{score}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>score</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{+\infty}\mathcal{L}_{SE}(s;t)\,\mathrm{d}t\leq\varepsilon^{\prime\prime}_{\mathrm{score}}</annotation></semantics></math>. First note that under <math id="A11.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{0}=\bm{\delta}_{\bm{a}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝜹</mi><mi>𝒂</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{0}=\bm{\delta}_{\bm{a}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A11.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{0}^{l}(\cdot|x_{0}^{\mathcal{M}_{k}^{c}})=\bm{\delta}^{l}_{\bm{a}^{l}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜹</mi><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{0}^{l}(\cdot|x_{0}^{\mathcal{M}_{k}^{c}})=\bm{\delta}^{l}_{\bm{a}^{l}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we can apply <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2. ‣ 4 Convergence Guarantees for the FHS Algorithm ‣ Sharp Convergence Rates for Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and compute the integrated <math id="A11.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{SE}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{SE}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows.</p>
<table id="A11.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A11.Ex159"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A11.Ex159.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{0}^{+\infty}\mathcal{L}_{SE}(s;t)\,\mathrm{d}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{0}^{+\infty}\mathcal{L}_{SE}(s;t)\,\mathrm{d}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A11.Ex159.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim q_{0}}[\mathcal{L}_{\infty}(x_{0})]-\sum_{k=1}^{d}\frac{1}{k}\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim q_{0}}\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{M}_{k}}\sum_{l\in\mathcal{M}_{k}}H\left(q_{0}^{l}(\cdot|x_{0}^{\mathcal{M}_{k}^{c}})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim q_{0}}[\mathcal{L}_{\infty}(x_{0})]-\sum_{k=1}^{d}\frac{1}{k}\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim q_{0}}\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{M}_{k}}\sum_{l\in\mathcal{M}_{k}}H\left(q_{0}^{l}(\cdot|x_{0}^{\mathcal{M}_{k}^{c}})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A11.Ex160"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A11.Ex160.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{L}_{\infty}(\bm{a})-0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{L}_{\infty}(\bm{a})-0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A11.Ex161"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A11.Ex161.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{+\infty}\frac{-\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\mathbb{E}_{q_{t|0}(x_{t}|\bm{a})}\left[\sum_{l:x_{t}^{l}=\mathrm{[MASK]}}\log\left(\mu_{\theta}^{l}(x_{t},t)[\bm{a}^{l}]\right)\right]\mathrm{d}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>MASK</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{+\infty}\frac{-\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\mathbb{E}_{q_{t|0}(x_{t}|\bm{a})}\left[\sum_{l:x_{t}^{l}=\mathrm{[MASK]}}\log\left(\mu_{\theta}^{l}(x_{t},t)[\bm{a}^{l}]\right)\right]\mathrm{d}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A11.Ex162"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A11.Ex162.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{+\infty}\frac{-\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\mathbb{E}_{q_{t|0}(x_{t}|\bm{a})}\left[\sum_{l:x_{t}^{l}=\mathrm{[MASK]}}\log\left(1-\rho\right)\right]\mathrm{d}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>MASK</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{+\infty}\frac{-\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\mathbb{E}_{q_{t|0}(x_{t}|\bm{a})}\left[\sum_{l:x_{t}^{l}=\mathrm{[MASK]}}\log\left(1-\rho\right)\right]\mathrm{d}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A11.Ex163"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A11.Ex163.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{+\infty}\frac{-\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\left(1-\rho\right)\mathbb{E}_{q_{t|0}(x_{t}|\bm{a})}\left[m(x_{t})\right]\mathrm{d}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{+\infty}\frac{-\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\left(1-\rho\right)\mathbb{E}_{q_{t|0}(x_{t}|\bm{a})}\left[m(x_{t})\right]\mathrm{d}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A11.Ex164"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A11.Ex164.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{+\infty}\frac{-\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\left(1-\rho\right)d(1-\alpha_{t})\mathrm{d}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{+\infty}\frac{-\alpha_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log\left(1-\rho\right)d(1-\alpha_{t})\mathrm{d}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A11.Ex165"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A11.Ex165.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-d\log(1-\rho)=\varepsilon^{\prime\prime}_{\mathrm{score}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>score</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-d\log(1-\rho)=\varepsilon^{\prime\prime}_{\mathrm{score}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A11.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A11.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the number of <math id="A11.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{[MASK]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>MASK</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{[MASK]}</annotation></semantics></math> tokens in <math id="A11.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the last inequality follows from the choice of <math id="A11.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A11.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A11.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Now, under FHS, since each token is predicted exactly once and <math id="A11.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> predicts the correct token <math id="A11.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> at each position <math id="A11.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> with the probability <math id="A11.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\rho)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A11.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{\mathrm{FHS}}(\bm{a})=(1-\rho)^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>FHS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{\mathrm{FHS}}(\bm{a})=(1-\rho)^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, since <math id="A11.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{0}=\bm{\delta}_{\bm{a}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝜹</mi><mi>𝒂</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{0}=\bm{\delta}_{\bm{a}}</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that</p>
<table id="A11.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A11.E39.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(q_{0}||\mathbb{P}_{\mathrm{FHS}})=-\log\left(\mathbb{P}_{\mathrm{FHS}}(a)\right)=-d\log(1-\rho)=\varepsilon^{\prime\prime}_{\mathrm{score}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>FHS</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>FHS</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>score</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(q_{0}||\mathbb{P}_{\mathrm{FHS}})=-\log\left(\mathbb{P}_{\mathrm{FHS}}(a)\right)=-d\log(1-\rho)=\varepsilon^{\prime\prime}_{\mathrm{score}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A11.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where the last inequality follows from the choice of <math id="A11.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A11.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A11.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The proof is now complete. Note that this special case with such a <math id="A11.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A11.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> indicates that the upper bound argued in <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4. ‣ 4 Convergence Guarantees for the FHS Algorithm ‣ Sharp Convergence Rates for Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> is tight.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A12" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix L </span>Proofs of Auxiliary Lemmas</h2>

<div id="A12.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide all the proofs for the auxiliary lemmas used in this paper.</p>
</div>
<section id="A12.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">L.1 </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ Appendix C Proof of ‣ Sharp Convergence Rates for Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A12.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that <math id="A12.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(T-t_{k})-(T-t_{k+1})=\kappa\min\left\{1,T-t_{k}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(T-t_{k})-(T-t_{k+1})=\kappa\min\left\{1,T-t_{k}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define <math id="A12.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{*}:=\sup\left\{k:T-t_{k}&gt;1\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{*}:=\sup\left\{k:T-t_{k}&gt;1\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>. We thus have the following cases.</p>
<ol id="A12.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A12.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A12.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Case 1: <math id="A12.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&lt;k^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&lt;k^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. This implies that <math id="A12.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T-t_{k}&gt;T-t_{k+1}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T-t_{k}&gt;T-t_{k+1}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A12.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{k+1}-t_{k}=\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{k+1}-t_{k}=\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we have</p>
<table id="A12.Ex166" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex166.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=0}^{k^{*}-1}\frac{(t_{k+1}-t_{k})^{p}}{\min\left\{1,T-t_{k+1}\right\}^{p}}=\kappa^{p}k^{*}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=0}^{k^{*}-1}\frac{(t_{k+1}-t_{k})^{p}}{\min\left\{1,T-t_{k+1}\right\}^{p}}=\kappa^{p}k^{*}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A12.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A12.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Case 2: <math id="A12.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;k^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;k^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. This implies that <math id="A12.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T-t_{k+1}&lt;T-t_{k}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T-t_{k+1}&lt;T-t_{k}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, and</p>
<table id="A12.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A12.Ex167"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.Ex167.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{k=k^{*}+1}^{N-1}\frac{(t_{k+1}-t_{k})^{p}}{\min\left\{1,T-t_{k+1}\right\}^{p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{k=k^{*}+1}^{N-1}\frac{(t_{k+1}-t_{k})^{p}}{\min\left\{1,T-t_{k+1}\right\}^{p}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.Ex167.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\kappa^{p}\sum_{k=k^{*}+1}^{N-1}\left(\frac{T-t_{k}}{T-t_{k+1}}\right)^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\kappa^{p}\sum_{k=k^{*}+1}^{N-1}\left(\frac{T-t_{k}}{T-t_{k+1}}\right)^{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A12.Ex168"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.Ex168.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\kappa^{p}\sum_{k=k^{*}+1}^{N-1}\left(\frac{1}{1-\kappa}\right)^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\kappa^{p}\sum_{k=k^{*}+1}^{N-1}\left(\frac{1}{1-\kappa}\right)^{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A12.Ex169"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.Ex169.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\asymp\kappa^{p}(N-k^{*}-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≍</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\asymp\kappa^{p}(N-k^{*}-1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the first line follows by definition of <math id="A12.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the last line follows due to the following. Note that for Case 2, the step-sizes satisfies that</p>
<table id="A12.Ex170" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex170.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T-t_{k}\leq T-t_{k+1}+\kappa." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T-t_{k}\leq T-t_{k+1}+\kappa.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.I1.i2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A12.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T-t_{k+1}\geq\delta^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T-t_{k+1}\geq\delta^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, this implies that <math id="A12.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq\frac{T-t_{k}}{T-t_{k+1}}=1+O(\kappa)=1+o(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq\frac{T-t_{k}}{T-t_{k+1}}=1+O(\kappa)=1+o(1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A12.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A12.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Case 3: <math id="A12.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=k^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=k^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. This implies that <math id="A12.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="T-t_{k+1}\in(1-\kappa,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T-t_{k+1}\in(1-\kappa,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A12.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="T-t_{k}\in(1,1+\kappa]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T-t_{k}\in(1,1+\kappa]</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A12.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{k+1}-t_{k}\leq\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{k+1}-t_{k}\leq\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>. For this case, we can similarly get <math id="A12.I1.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{T-t_{k}}{T-t_{k+1}}=1+o(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{T-t_{k}}{T-t_{k+1}}=1+o(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, and thus</p>
<table id="A12.Ex171" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex171.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{(t_{k+1}-t_{k})^{p}}{\min\left\{1,T-t_{k+1}\right\}^{p}}=\kappa^{p}(1+o(1))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{(t_{k+1}-t_{k})^{p}}{\min\left\{1,T-t_{k+1}\right\}^{p}}=\kappa^{p}(1+o(1)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A12.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Summing up all three cases, we have</p>
<table id="A12.Ex172" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex172.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}\frac{(t_{k+1}-t_{k})^{p}}{\min\left\{1,T-t_{k+1}\right\}^{p}}\asymp\kappa^{p}N." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≍</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}\frac{(t_{k+1}-t_{k})^{p}}{\min\left\{1,T-t_{k+1}\right\}^{p}}\asymp\kappa^{p}N.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A12.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we need to determine the total number of steps. When <math id="A12.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leq k^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leq k^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, the number of steps is simply</p>
<table id="A12.Ex173" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex173.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{*}=:N_{1}=\left\lfloor\frac{T-1}{\kappa}\right\rfloor\asymp\frac{T}{\kappa}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>κ</mi></mfrac><mo>⌋</mo></mrow><mo>≍</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mi>κ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{*}=:N_{1}=\left\lfloor\frac{T-1}{\kappa}\right\rfloor\asymp\frac{T}{\kappa}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A12.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;k^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;k^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, in order to reach that <math id="A12.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T-t_{N}\asymp\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≍</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T-t_{N}\asymp\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, we need</p>
<table id="A12.Ex174" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex174.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{2}\asymp\log_{1-\kappa}\delta\asymp\frac{\log\delta^{-1}}{\kappa}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≍</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>≍</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mi>κ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{2}\asymp\log_{1-\kappa}\delta\asymp\frac{\log\delta^{-1}}{\kappa}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Therefore, the total number of steps satisfies that</p>
<table id="A12.Ex175" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex175.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=N_{1}+N_{2}\asymp\frac{T+\log\delta^{-1}}{\kappa}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≍</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mi>κ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=N_{1}+N_{2}\asymp\frac{T+\log\delta^{-1}}{\kappa}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.SS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">The proof is now complete.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A12.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">L.2 </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ Appendix D Proof of ‣ Sharp Convergence Rates for Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A12.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Before we dive into the proof, we provide some intuition for our result. Intuitively, the instantaneous change of the indicator function should only be non-zero for those <math id="A12.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> on the boundary (i.e., where <math id="A12.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t}(x)=p_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mpadded style="width:6.5pt;height:7.1pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;" depth="0.0pt" height="7.1pt" width="6.5pt"><mover accent="true"><mpadded style="width:4.8pt;height:6.199999999999999pt;vertical-align:-1.9pt;" depth="1.9pt" height="4.3pt" width="4.8pt"><mi>q</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mpadded><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t}(x)=p_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>). As a result, this second term should be exactly zero. This is characterized by the following lemma.</p>
</div>
<div id="A12.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Write <math id="A12.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{t}:=\{x:\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t}(x)\neq p_{t}(x)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.448em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mpadded style="width:6.5pt;height:7.1pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;" depth="0.0pt" height="7.1pt" width="6.5pt"><mover accent="true"><mpadded style="width:4.8pt;height:6.199999999999999pt;vertical-align:-1.9pt;" depth="1.9pt" height="4.3pt" width="4.8pt"><mi>q</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mpadded><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{t}:=\{x:\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t}(x)\neq p_{t}(x)\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose that we can show that for all such <math id="A12.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\Phi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\Phi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A12.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{\partial}{\partial t}\mathds{1}\left\{\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t}(x)&gt;p_{t}(x)\right\}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">{</mo><msub><mpadded style="width:6.5pt;height:7.1pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;" depth="0.0pt" height="7.1pt" width="6.5pt"><mover accent="true"><mpadded style="width:4.8pt;height:6.199999999999999pt;vertical-align:-1.9pt;" depth="1.9pt" height="4.3pt" width="4.8pt"><mi>q</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mpadded><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial}{\partial t}\mathds{1}\left\{\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t}(x)&gt;p_{t}(x)\right\}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then the result is obvious.</p>
</div>
<div id="A12.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Now fix <math id="A12.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\Phi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\Phi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. From the Kolmogorov forward equation, we have</p>
<table id="A12.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A12.Ex176"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.Ex176.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t+\Delta t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mpadded style="width:6.5pt;height:7.1pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;" depth="0.0pt" height="7.1pt" width="6.5pt"><mover accent="true"><mpadded style="width:4.8pt;height:6.199999999999999pt;vertical-align:-1.9pt;" depth="1.9pt" height="4.3pt" width="4.8pt"><mi>q</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mpadded><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t+\Delta t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.Ex176.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{y\in\mathcal{X}}\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t}(y)\left(\mathds{1}\left\{y=x\right\}+\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle R\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle R\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle R\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle R\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t}(y,x)\Delta t\right)+o(\Delta t)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mpadded style="width:6.5pt;height:7.1pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;" depth="0.0pt" height="7.1pt" width="6.5pt"><mover accent="true"><mpadded style="width:4.8pt;height:6.199999999999999pt;vertical-align:-1.9pt;" depth="1.9pt" height="4.3pt" width="4.8pt"><mi>q</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mpadded><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.392em">+</mo><msub><mpadded style="width:6.5pt;height:7.1pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;" depth="0.0pt" height="7.1pt" width="6.5pt"><mover accent="true"><mpadded style="width:7.7pt;height:6.8pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;" depth="0.0pt" height="6.8pt" width="7.7pt"><mi>R</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mpadded><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{y\in\mathcal{X}}\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t}(y)\left(\mathds{1}\left\{y=x\right\}+\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle R\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle R\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle R\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle R\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t}(y,x)\Delta t\right)+o(\Delta t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A12.Ex177"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.Ex177.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{t+\Delta t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{t+\Delta t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.Ex177.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{y\in\mathcal{X}}p_{t}(y)\left(\mathds{1}\left\{y=x\right\}+\hat{R}_{t}(y,x)\Delta t\right)+o(\Delta t)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{y\in\mathcal{X}}p_{t}(y)\left(\mathds{1}\left\{y=x\right\}+\hat{R}_{t}(y,x)\Delta t\right)+o(\Delta t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Thus,</p>
<table id="A12.Ex178" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex178.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t+\Delta t}(x)-p_{t+\Delta t}(x)=\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t}(x)-p_{t}(x)+O(\Delta t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mpadded style="width:6.5pt;height:7.1pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;" depth="0.0pt" height="7.1pt" width="6.5pt"><mover accent="true"><mpadded style="width:4.8pt;height:6.199999999999999pt;vertical-align:-1.9pt;" depth="1.9pt" height="4.3pt" width="4.8pt"><mi>q</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mpadded><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.448em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mpadded style="width:6.5pt;height:7.1pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;" depth="0.0pt" height="7.1pt" width="6.5pt"><mover accent="true"><mpadded style="width:4.8pt;height:6.199999999999999pt;vertical-align:-1.9pt;" depth="1.9pt" height="4.3pt" width="4.8pt"><mi>q</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mpadded><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t+\Delta t}(x)-p_{t+\Delta t}(x)=\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t}(x)-p_{t}(x)+O(\Delta t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">We now divide into the following two cases within <math id="A12.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. The first case is where <math id="A12.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t}(x)&gt;p_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mpadded style="width:6.5pt;height:7.1pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;" depth="0.0pt" height="7.1pt" width="6.5pt"><mover accent="true"><mpadded style="width:4.8pt;height:6.199999999999999pt;vertical-align:-1.9pt;" depth="1.9pt" height="4.3pt" width="4.8pt"><mi>q</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mpadded><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t}(x)&gt;p_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A12.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> is discrete, there exists some <math id="A12.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{t}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{t}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A12.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t}(x)-p_{t}(x)\geq\epsilon_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mpadded style="width:6.5pt;height:7.1pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;" depth="0.0pt" height="7.1pt" width="6.5pt"><mover accent="true"><mpadded style="width:4.8pt;height:6.199999999999999pt;vertical-align:-1.9pt;" depth="1.9pt" height="4.3pt" width="4.8pt"><mi>q</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mpadded><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t}(x)-p_{t}(x)\geq\epsilon_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for vanishing <math id="A12.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A12.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t+\Delta t}(x)-p_{t+\Delta t}(x)\geq\epsilon_{t}-O(\Delta t)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mpadded style="width:6.5pt;height:7.1pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;" depth="0.0pt" height="7.1pt" width="6.5pt"><mover accent="true"><mpadded style="width:4.8pt;height:6.199999999999999pt;vertical-align:-1.9pt;" depth="1.9pt" height="4.3pt" width="4.8pt"><mi>q</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mpadded><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t+\Delta t}(x)-p_{t+\Delta t}(x)\geq\epsilon_{t}-O(\Delta t)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. The second case is where <math id="A12.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t}(x)&lt;p_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mpadded style="width:6.5pt;height:7.1pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;" depth="0.0pt" height="7.1pt" width="6.5pt"><mover accent="true"><mpadded style="width:4.8pt;height:6.199999999999999pt;vertical-align:-1.9pt;" depth="1.9pt" height="4.3pt" width="4.8pt"><mi>q</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mpadded><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t}(x)&lt;p_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. With a similar argument, we get <math id="A12.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t+\Delta t}(x)&lt;p_{t+\Delta t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mpadded style="width:6.5pt;height:7.1pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;" depth="0.0pt" height="7.1pt" width="6.5pt"><mover accent="true"><mpadded style="width:4.8pt;height:6.199999999999999pt;vertical-align:-1.9pt;" depth="1.9pt" height="4.3pt" width="4.8pt"><mi>q</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mpadded><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t+\Delta t}(x)&lt;p_{t+\Delta t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. For both cases, we get, for vanishing <math id="A12.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A12.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\Phi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\Phi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A12.Ex179" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex179.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathds{1}\left\{\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t+\Delta t}(x)&gt;p_{t+\Delta t}(x)\right\}=\mathds{1}\left\{\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t}(x)&gt;p_{t}(x)\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">{</mo><msub><mpadded style="width:6.5pt;height:7.1pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;" depth="0.0pt" height="7.1pt" width="6.5pt"><mover accent="true"><mpadded style="width:4.8pt;height:6.199999999999999pt;vertical-align:-1.9pt;" depth="1.9pt" height="4.3pt" width="4.8pt"><mi>q</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mpadded><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">{</mo><msub><mpadded style="width:6.5pt;height:7.1pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;" depth="0.0pt" height="7.1pt" width="6.5pt"><mover accent="true"><mpadded style="width:4.8pt;height:6.199999999999999pt;vertical-align:-1.9pt;" depth="1.9pt" height="4.3pt" width="4.8pt"><mi>q</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mpadded><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathds{1}\left\{\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t+\Delta t}(x)&gt;p_{t+\Delta t}(x)\right\}=\mathds{1}\left\{\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t}(x)&gt;p_{t}(x)\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p">The proof is now complete.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A12.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">L.3 </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ E.2 Step 2: Upper-bound initialization error ‣ Appendix E Proof of ‣ Sharp Convergence Rates for Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></h3>

<div id="A12.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="A12.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0}=\bm{\delta}_{\mathrm{[MASK]}^{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝜹</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>MASK</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0}=\bm{\delta}_{\mathrm{[MASK]}^{d}}</annotation></semantics></math> if we use the absorbing rate matrix. Also, a useful result under the absorbing-rate is that we can explicitly write the forward conditional probability as</p>
<table id="A12.E40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t|0}(x|x_{0})=(1-e^{-t})^{\sum_{i}\mathds{1}\left\{x^{i}=\mathrm{[MASK]},x_{0}^{i}\neq\mathrm{[MASK]}\right\}}\\
\cdot(e^{-t})^{\sum_{i}\mathds{1}\left\{x^{i}=x_{0}^{i}\neq\mathrm{[MASK]}\right\}}\cdot 0^{\sum_{i}\mathds{1}\left\{x^{i}\neq\mathrm{[MASK]},x^{i}\neq x_{0}^{i}\right\}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>MASK</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>MASK</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mo>{</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>≠</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>MASK</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>}</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>0</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>MASK</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>≠</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t|0}(x|x_{0})=(1-e^{-t})^{\sum_{i}\mathds{1}\left\{x^{i}=\mathrm{[MASK]},x_{0}^{i}\neq\mathrm{[MASK]}\right\}}\\
\cdot(e^{-t})^{\sum_{i}\mathds{1}\left\{x^{i}=x_{0}^{i}\neq\mathrm{[MASK]}\right\}}\cdot 0^{\sum_{i}\mathds{1}\left\{x^{i}\neq\mathrm{[MASK]},x^{i}\neq x_{0}^{i}\right\}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A12.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Thus,</p>
<table id="A12.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A12.Ex180"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.Ex180.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{TV}(q_{T},p_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{TV}(q_{T},p_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.Ex180.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{x:p_{0}&gt;q_{T}}p_{0}(x)-q_{T}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{x:p_{0}&gt;q_{T}}p_{0}(x)-q_{T}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A12.Ex181"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.Ex181.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle(i)}}{{=}}p_{0}(\mathrm{[MASK]}^{d})-q_{T}(\mathrm{[MASK]}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mover><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>MASK</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>MASK</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle(i)}}{{=}}p_{0}(\mathrm{[MASK]}^{d})-q_{T}(\mathrm{[MASK]}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A12.Ex182"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.Ex182.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle(ii)}}{{=}}1-\sum_{x_{0}\in\mathcal{X}}q_{0}(x_{0})(1-e^{-T})^{\sum_{i}\mathds{1}\left\{x_{0}^{i}\neq\mathrm{[MASK]}\right\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mover><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mo>{</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>≠</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>MASK</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>}</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle(ii)}}{{=}}1-\sum_{x_{0}\in\mathcal{X}}q_{0}(x_{0})(1-e^{-T})^{\sum_{i}\mathds{1}\left\{x_{0}^{i}\neq\mathrm{[MASK]}\right\}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A12.Ex183"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.Ex183.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 1-(1-e^{-T})^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 1-(1-e^{-T})^{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A12.Ex184"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.Ex184.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim de^{-T}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim de^{-T},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A12.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i)</annotation></semantics></math> follows because <math id="A12.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is a singleton at <math id="A12.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{[MASK]}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>MASK</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{[MASK]}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A12.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(ii)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(ii)</annotation></semantics></math> follows from (<a href="#A12.E40" title="Equation 40 ‣ L.3 Proof of ‣ Appendix L Proofs of Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Sharp Convergence Rates for Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A12.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">L.4 </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ E.3 Step 3: Upper-bound discretization error ‣ Appendix E Proof of ‣ Sharp Convergence Rates for Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></h3>

<div id="A12.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proof is similar to Lemma 1 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite>. The only difference is a different definition for <math id="A12.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. We provide the proof here for completeness.</p>
<table id="A12.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A12.Ex185"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.Ex185.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{t}\sim\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t}\\
x_{t_{k}}\sim\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t_{k}}\end{subarray}}\left[h_{t}(x_{t})-h_{t}(x_{t_{k}})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.388em">∼</mo><msub><mpadded style="width:6.5pt;height:7.1pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;" depth="0.0pt" height="7.1pt" width="6.5pt"><mover accent="true"><mpadded style="width:1.7pt;height:2.2pt;vertical-align:-0.7pt;" depth="0.7pt" height="1.5pt" width="1.7pt"><mi mathsize="0.480em">q</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mpadded><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.388em">∼</mo><msub><mpadded style="width:6.5pt;height:7.1pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;" depth="0.0pt" height="7.1pt" width="6.5pt"><mover accent="true"><mpadded style="width:1.7pt;height:2.2pt;vertical-align:-0.7pt;" depth="0.7pt" height="1.5pt" width="1.7pt"><mi mathsize="0.480em">q</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mpadded><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{t}\sim\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t}\\
x_{t_{k}}\sim\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t_{k}}\end{subarray}}\left[h_{t}(x_{t})-h_{t}(x_{t_{k}})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A12.Ex186"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.Ex186.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t}}\left[h_{t}(x_{t})-\sum_{x_{t_{k}}\in[S]^{d}}q_{T-t_{k}|T-t}(x_{t_{k}}|x_{t})h_{t}(x_{t_{k}})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.388em">∼</mo><msub><mpadded style="width:6.5pt;height:7.1pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;" depth="0.0pt" height="7.1pt" width="6.5pt"><mover accent="true"><mpadded style="width:1.7pt;height:2.2pt;vertical-align:-0.7pt;" depth="0.7pt" height="1.5pt" width="1.7pt"><mi mathsize="0.480em">q</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mpadded><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t}}\left[h_{t}(x_{t})-\sum_{x_{t_{k}}\in[S]^{d}}q_{T-t_{k}|T-t}(x_{t_{k}}|x_{t})h_{t}(x_{t_{k}})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A12.Ex187"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.Ex187.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t}}\left[h_{t}(x_{t})-\sum_{x_{t_{k}}\in[S]^{d}}\left(\mathds{1}\left\{x_{t_{k}}=x_{t}\right\}+R_{t}(x_{t},x_{t_{k}})(t-t_{k})\right)h_{t}(x_{t_{k}})\right]+o(t-t_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.388em">∼</mo><msub><mpadded style="width:6.5pt;height:7.1pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;" depth="0.0pt" height="7.1pt" width="6.5pt"><mover accent="true"><mpadded style="width:1.7pt;height:2.2pt;vertical-align:-0.7pt;" depth="0.7pt" height="1.5pt" width="1.7pt"><mi mathsize="0.480em">q</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mpadded><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t}}\left[h_{t}(x_{t})-\sum_{x_{t_{k}}\in[S]^{d}}\left(\mathds{1}\left\{x_{t_{k}}=x_{t}\right\}+R_{t}(x_{t},x_{t_{k}})(t-t_{k})\right)h_{t}(x_{t_{k}})\right]+o(t-t_{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A12.Ex188"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.Ex188.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=(t-t_{k})\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t}}\left[-\sum_{x_{t_{k}}\in[S]^{d}}R_{t}(x_{t},x_{t_{k}})h_{t}(x_{t_{k}})\right]+o(t-t_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.388em">∼</mo><msub><mpadded style="width:6.5pt;height:7.1pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;" depth="0.0pt" height="7.1pt" width="6.5pt"><mover accent="true"><mpadded style="width:1.7pt;height:2.2pt;vertical-align:-0.7pt;" depth="0.7pt" height="1.5pt" width="1.7pt"><mi mathsize="0.480em">q</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mpadded><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(t-t_{k})\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t}}\left[-\sum_{x_{t_{k}}\in[S]^{d}}R_{t}(x_{t},x_{t_{k}})h_{t}(x_{t_{k}})\right]+o(t-t_{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A12.Ex189"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.Ex189.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle(i)}}{{\leq}}(t-t_{k})\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t}}\left[(-R_{t}(x_{t},x_{t}))h_{t}(x_{t})\right]+o(t-t_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mover><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.388em">∼</mo><msub><mpadded style="width:6.5pt;height:7.1pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;" depth="0.0pt" height="7.1pt" width="6.5pt"><mover accent="true"><mpadded style="width:1.7pt;height:2.2pt;vertical-align:-0.7pt;" depth="0.7pt" height="1.5pt" width="1.7pt"><mi mathsize="0.480em">q</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></mpadded><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle(i)}}{{\leq}}(t-t_{k})\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim\mathchoice{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\displaystyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\displaystyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 3.0mu\reflectbox{$\textstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-3.0mu\textstyle q\mkern 3.0mu$}}$}\mkern-3.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}{\mkern 2.0mu\reflectbox{$\scriptscriptstyle\vec{\reflectbox{$\mkern-2.0mu\scriptscriptstyle q\mkern 2.0mu$}}$}\mkern-2.0mu}_{t}}\left[(-R_{t}(x_{t},x_{t}))h_{t}(x_{t})\right]+o(t-t_{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A12.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i)</annotation></semantics></math> follows because <math id="A12.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{t}(x)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{t}(x)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A12.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t}(x,y)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t}(x,y)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A12.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\neq y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\neq y</annotation></semantics></math>. Now, for uniform-rate, we have <math id="A12.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R_{t}(x,x)=-\sum_{y:y\neq x}R_{t}(x,y)=-\frac{S-1}{S}d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></mfrac><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t}(x,x)=-\sum_{y:y\neq x}R_{t}(x,y)=-\frac{S-1}{S}d</annotation></semantics></math>. Also, for absorbing-rate, we have <math id="A12.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R_{t}(x,x)=-\sum_{y:y\neq x}R_{t}(x,y)=-(d-m(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t}(x,x)=-\sum_{y:y\neq x}R_{t}(x,y)=-(d-m(x))</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A12.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(x)\penalty\ (\leq d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:0.889em;" width="0.889em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(x)\penalty\ (\leq d)</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of mask states in <math id="A12.SS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. We have the desired result for both cases.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A12.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">L.5 </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmlemma5" title="Lemma 5. ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix I FHS Sampling in CTMC Framework: and its Proof ‣ Sharp Convergence Rates for Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a></h3>

<div id="A12.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(1) Instantaneous total rate of leaving <math id="A12.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="A12.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> For any <math id="A12.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A12.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\neq y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\neq y</annotation></semantics></math>, the reverse CTMC process
satisfies the local transition given by</p>
<table id="A12.E41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(Y_{t-dt}=y\mid Y_{t}=x)=\widetilde{R}_{t}(x,y)\,dt+o(dt)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(Y_{t-dt}=y\mid Y_{t}=x)=\widetilde{R}_{t}(x,y)\,dt+o(dt).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Taking summation over all <math id="A12.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\neq x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\neq x</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</p>
<table id="A12.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(Y_{t-dt}\neq x\mid Y_{t}=x)=\sum_{y\neq x}\widetilde{R}_{t}(x,y)\,dt+o(dt)=\Lambda(t,x)\,dt+o(dt)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(Y_{t-dt}\neq x\mid Y_{t}=x)=\sum_{y\neq x}\widetilde{R}_{t}(x,y)\,dt+o(dt)=\Lambda(t,x)\,dt+o(dt),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.SS5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A12.Ex190" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex190.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda(t,x)=\sum_{y\neq x}\widetilde{R}_{t}(x,y)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda(t,x)=\sum_{y\neq x}\widetilde{R}_{t}(x,y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.SS5.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Thus <math id="A12.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda(t,x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda(t,x)</annotation></semantics></math> is the instantaneous rate of leaving
state <math id="A12.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="A12.SS5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A12.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(2) Unmasking time <math id="A12.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> in state <math id="A12.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
Fix <math id="A12.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A12.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, and define the survival function</p>
<table id="A12.Ex191" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex191.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(h):=\mathbb{P}(\tau&lt;t-h\mid Y_{t}=x),\qquad h\geq 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(h):=\mathbb{P}(\tau&lt;t-h\mid Y_{t}=x),\qquad h\geq 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.SS5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A12.Ex192" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex192.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau:=\sup\{s&lt;t:Y_{s}\neq x\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau:=\sup\{s&lt;t:Y_{s}\neq x\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.SS5.p2.3" class="ltx_p">is the first unmasking time after <math id="A12.SS5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> for the reverse process indexed by the forward time.</p>
</div>
<div id="A12.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To derive a differential equation for <math id="A12.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(h)</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A12.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be a small constant, and <math id="A12.SS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}_{\{\cdot\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}_{\{\cdot\}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the indicator function. Using the Markov property at time <math id="A12.SS5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t-h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t-h</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A12.Ex193" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A12.Ex193X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.Ex193X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S(h+\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S(h+\delta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.Ex193X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}(\tau&lt;t-h-\delta|Y_{t}=x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}(\tau&lt;t-h-\delta|Y_{t}=x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A12.Ex193Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.Ex193Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\tau}\left[\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&lt;t-h\}}\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&lt;t-h-\delta\}}|Y_{t}=x\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>[</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\tau}\left[\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&lt;t-h\}}\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&lt;t-h-\delta\}}|Y_{t}=x\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A12.Ex193Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.Ex193Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{Y_{t-h}}\left[\mathbb{E}_{\tau|Y_{t-h}}\left[\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&lt;t-h\}}\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&lt;t-h-\delta\}}|Y_{t-h},Y_{t}=x\right]|Y_{t}=x\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>]</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{Y_{t-h}}\left[\mathbb{E}_{\tau|Y_{t-h}}\left[\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&lt;t-h\}}\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&lt;t-h-\delta\}}|Y_{t-h},Y_{t}=x\right]|Y_{t}=x\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A12.Ex193Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.Ex193Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(i)}{=}\mathbb{E}_{Y_{t-h}}\left[\mathbb{E}_{\tau|Y_{t-h}}\left[\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&lt;t-h\}}\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&lt;t-h-\delta\}}|Y_{t-h}=x,Y_{t}=x\right]|Y_{t}=x\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>]</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(i)}{=}\mathbb{E}_{Y_{t-h}}\left[\mathbb{E}_{\tau|Y_{t-h}}\left[\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&lt;t-h\}}\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&lt;t-h-\delta\}}|Y_{t-h}=x,Y_{t}=x\right]|Y_{t}=x\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A12.Ex193Xd"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.Ex193Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(ii)}{=}\mathbb{E}_{Y_{t-h}}\left[\mathbb{E}_{\tau|Y_{t-h}}\left[\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&lt;t-h\}}|Y_{t-h}=x,Y_{t}=x\right]\mathbb{P}(\tau&lt;t-h-\delta|Y_{t-h}=x)|Y_{t}=x\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>]</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(ii)}{=}\mathbb{E}_{Y_{t-h}}\left[\mathbb{E}_{\tau|Y_{t-h}}\left[\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&lt;t-h\}}|Y_{t-h}=x,Y_{t}=x\right]\mathbb{P}(\tau&lt;t-h-\delta|Y_{t-h}=x)|Y_{t}=x\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A12.Ex193Xe"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.Ex193Xe.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{Y_{t-h}}\left[\mathbb{E}_{\tau|Y_{t-h}}\left[\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&lt;t-h\}}|Y_{t-h}=x,Y_{t}=x\right]|Y_{t}=x\right]\mathbb{P}(\tau&lt;t-h-\delta|Y_{t-h}=x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>]</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>]</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{Y_{t-h}}\left[\mathbb{E}_{\tau|Y_{t-h}}\left[\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&lt;t-h\}}|Y_{t-h}=x,Y_{t}=x\right]|Y_{t}=x\right]\mathbb{P}(\tau&lt;t-h-\delta|Y_{t-h}=x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A12.Ex193Xf"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.Ex193Xf.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(iii)}{=}\mathbb{E}_{Y_{t-h}}\left[\mathbb{E}_{\tau|Y_{t-h}}\left[\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&lt;t-h\}}|Y_{t-h},Y_{t}=x\right]|Y_{t}=x\right]\mathbb{P}(\tau&lt;t-h-\delta|Y_{t-h}=x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>]</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>]</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(iii)}{=}\mathbb{E}_{Y_{t-h}}\left[\mathbb{E}_{\tau|Y_{t-h}}\left[\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&lt;t-h\}}|Y_{t-h},Y_{t}=x\right]|Y_{t}=x\right]\mathbb{P}(\tau&lt;t-h-\delta|Y_{t-h}=x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A12.Ex193Xg"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.Ex193Xg.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\tau}\left[\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&lt;t-h\}}|Y_{t}=x\right]\mathbb{P}(\tau&lt;t-h-\delta|Y_{t-h}=x)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>[</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>]</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\tau}\left[\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&lt;t-h\}}|Y_{t}=x\right]\mathbb{P}(\tau&lt;t-h-\delta|Y_{t-h}=x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.SS5.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="A12.SS5.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i)</annotation></semantics></math> follows because <math id="A12.SS5.p3.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&lt;t-h\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&lt;t-h\}}</annotation></semantics></math> is non-zero only when <math id="A12.SS5.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{t-h}=Y_{t}=x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{t-h}=Y_{t}=x</annotation></semantics></math>. Also, <math id="A12.SS5.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(ii)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(ii)</annotation></semantics></math> follows because <math id="A12.SS5.p3.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&lt;t-h\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&lt;t-h\}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a (deterministic) function of <math id="A12.SS5.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{t-h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{t-h}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A12.SS5.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Also, by Markov property, <math id="A12.SS5.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\tau&lt;t-h-\delta|Y_{t-h},Y_{t})=\mathbb{P}(\tau&lt;t-h-\delta|Y_{t-h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\tau&lt;t-h-\delta|Y_{t-h},Y_{t})=\mathbb{P}(\tau&lt;t-h-\delta|Y_{t-h})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, <math id="A12.SS5.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(iii)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(iii)</annotation></semantics></math> follows again because <math id="A12.SS5.p3.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&lt;t-h\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&lt;t-h\}}</annotation></semantics></math> is non-zero only when <math id="A12.SS5.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{t-h}=Y_{t}=x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{t-h}=Y_{t}=x</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus,</p>
<table id="A12.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A12.Ex194"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.Ex194.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S(h+\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S(h+\delta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.Ex194.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=S(h)\,\mathbb{P}(\tau&lt;t-h-\delta\mid Y_{t-h}=x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=S(h)\,\mathbb{P}(\tau&lt;t-h-\delta\mid Y_{t-h}=x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A12.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=S(h)\big(1-\Lambda(t-h,x)\,\delta+o(\delta)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=S(h)\big(1-\Lambda(t-h,x)\,\delta+o(\delta)\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.SS5.p3.3" class="ltx_p">where the second equality follows because given <math id="A12.SS5.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{t-h}=x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{t-h}=x</annotation></semantics></math>, the condition <math id="A12.SS5.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau&lt;t-h-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau&lt;t-h-\delta</annotation></semantics></math> exactly defines the process that does not leave <math id="A12.SS5.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A12.SS5.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[t-h-\delta,\,t-h]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[t-h-\delta,\,t-h]</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence
(<a href="#A12.E42" title="Equation 42 ‣ L.5 Proof of ‣ Appendix L Proofs of Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Sharp Convergence Rates for Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>) yields</p>
<table id="A12.Ex195" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex195.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\tau&lt;t-h-\delta\mid Y_{t-h}=x)=1-\Lambda(t-h,x)\,\delta+o(\delta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\tau&lt;t-h-\delta\mid Y_{t-h}=x)=1-\Lambda(t-h,x)\,\delta+o(\delta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A12.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.SS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Equation (<a href="#A12.E43" title="Equation 43 ‣ L.5 Proof of ‣ Appendix L Proofs of Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Sharp Convergence Rates for Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>) further yields</p>
<table id="A12.Ex196" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex196.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{S(h+\delta)-S(h)}{\delta}=-\Lambda(t-h,x)\,S(h)+o(1)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{S(h+\delta)-S(h)}{\delta}=-\Lambda(t-h,x)\,S(h)+o(1),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.SS5.p4.2" class="ltx_p">which implies the following ODE as <math id="A12.SS5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A12.Ex197" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex197.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}(h)=-\Lambda(t-h,x)\,S(h),\qquad S(0)=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}(h)=-\Lambda(t-h,x)\,S(h),\qquad S(0)=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.SS5.p4.3" class="ltx_p">Solving the above ODE, we get</p>
<table id="A12.Ex198" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex198.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="S(h)=\exp\!\Big(-\int_{h}^{0}\Lambda(t-u,x)\,du\Big)=\exp\!\Big(-\int_{t-h}^{t}\Lambda(u,x)\,du\Big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(h)=\exp\!\Big(-\int_{h}^{0}\Lambda(t-u,x)\,du\Big)=\exp\!\Big(-\int_{t-h}^{t}\Lambda(u,x)\,du\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.SS5.p4.4" class="ltx_p">which completes the proof of the second claim.</p>
</div>
<div id="A12.SS5.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.SS5.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(3) Distribution of the predicted token.</span>
We first derive:</p>
<table id="A12.Ex199" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A12.Ex199X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.Ex199X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℙ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A12.Ex199X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(Y_{\tau}=y\mid Y_{t}=x,\tau\in(t-\delta,t])=\frac{\mathbb{(}Y_{\tau}=y\mid Y_{t}=x)}{\mathbb{P}(Y_{\tau}\neq x\mid Y_{t}=x)}=\frac{\widetilde{R}_{t}(x,y)\delta+o(\delta)}{\Lambda(t,x)\delta+o(\delta)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(Y_{\tau}=y\mid Y_{t}=x,\tau\in(t-\delta,t])=\frac{\mathbb{(}Y_{\tau}=y\mid Y_{t}=x)}{\mathbb{P}(Y_{\tau}\neq x\mid Y_{t}=x)}=\frac{\widetilde{R}_{t}(x,y)\delta+o(\delta)}{\Lambda(t,x)\delta+o(\delta)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A12.SS5.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.SS5.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Then, letting <math id="A12.SS5.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\downarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\downarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A12.Ex200" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex200.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lim\limits_{\delta\downarrow 0}\ \mathbb{P}(Y_{\tau}=y\mid Y_{t}=x,\tau\in(t-\delta,t])=\frac{\widetilde{R}_{t}(x,y)}{\Lambda(t,x)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim\limits_{\delta\downarrow 0}\ \mathbb{P}(Y_{\tau}=y\mid Y_{t}=x,\tau\in(t-\delta,t])=\frac{\widetilde{R}_{t}(x,y)}{\Lambda(t,x)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.SS5.p6.2" class="ltx_p">which implies the distribution of next state.
The proof is now complete.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A12.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">L.6 </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmlemma6" title="Lemma 6. ‣ Appendix J Proof of ‣ Sharp Convergence Rates for Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a></h3>

<div id="A12.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following from the proof of Proposition 4.1 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>]</cite>, we have</p>
<table id="A12.Ex201" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex201.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\alpha_{\tau_{k-1}}=u_{(k)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\alpha_{\tau_{k-1}}=u_{(k)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.SS6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A12.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{u_{(k)}\}_{k=1}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{u_{(k)}\}_{k=1}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> are order statistics of <math id="A12.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> independent and uniformly distributed variables on <math id="A12.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, satisfying <math id="A12.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{(d)}&gt;\cdots&gt;u_{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">&gt;</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">&gt;</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{(d)}&gt;\cdots&gt;u_{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math>. It is well known that the <math id="A12.SS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th order statistic of <math id="A12.SS6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> i.i.d. random variables with the distribution of <math id="A12.SS6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Unif}\;(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Unif</mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Unif}\;(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> follows a <math id="A12.SS6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Beta(k,d+1-k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Beta(k,d+1-k)</annotation></semantics></math> distribution given by</p>
<table id="A12.Ex202" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex202.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{(k)}\sim Beta(k,d+1-k)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{(k)}\sim Beta(k,d+1-k).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A12.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We use the following fact for the Beta distribution. Suppose that <math id="A12.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim Beta(a,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim Beta(a,b)</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A12.SS6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-X\sim Beta(b,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-X\sim Beta(b,a)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, we obtain the distribution of <math id="A12.SS6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\tau_{k-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\tau_{k-1}}</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="A12.Ex203" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex203.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\tau_{k-1}}\sim Beta(d+1-k,k)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\tau_{k-1}}\sim Beta(d+1-k,k).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A12.SS6.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.SS6.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The proof is now complete.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</article>
</div>
</div>
